## Summary
A research team from Sahmyook University led by Professor Lee Yong-woo has scientifically validated the effectiveness of virtual reality (VR) in physical therapy education. The study demonstrates that VR-based methods can enhance learning outcomes for physical therapy students, with potential implications for improving educational practices in healthcare.

## Key Points
- Scientific proof of VR effectiveness in physical therapy education.
- Research conducted by a team from Sahmyook University under Professor Lee Yong-woo.
- VR technology can enhance training and learning in healthcare fields.
- Findings may lead to improved educational tools for medical professionals.
- Contribution to advancements in medical education through innovative methods.


